- Exact current floor builder is promoted `2c428ad55872116a8e3b6e180eafd93e5502ddb6afde63a495fb2ba4684d5dee`; adopted current manifest is `dbfae4cb27b98ede81761ed19c4b63b6d7f3f65410e202e0a02b872dff5139a5`. Historical candidate manifest `f5e5c203…`, old art `ef54d6df…`/manifest `4610d217…`, and native1 665/0 evidence are not relabeled.

`git apply --check` passed against the actual untouched 523-line target. A separate in-memory unified-hunk replay reproduced the candidate exactly. These are text checks only; no parser, native engine, promotion, visual/Save acceptance or new pass is claimed. Existing recorded evidence and prior private artifacts are untouched. Suggested owner invocation retains the canonical queue, with this existing script and user argument `--floor-resource-guards-only`; the owner remains responsible for the exact command/run recorder.

## Actual construction and state authority

The selector reuses `_aggregate_start` unchanged: real isolated production CampaignShell Title/Settings Standard/Journey/Begin and public TEST predecessor completion/contact construct actual A1-L3 at spawn, with one actual Player, one Scheduler and all nineteen retained initially dormant sources. These TEST metadata handoffs are setup only. The pristine snapshot is the existing canonical paused capture, with empty native encounter/profile/leases/framing, no fields/consumers and no actual swipe/primary. The new branch never seeds HP, ammo, grounded flags, phase, motion, history, epochs or progress and never installs a candidate.

`_floor_resource_guards` at candidate line 497 calls canonical Shell `_prepare_snapshot(pristine)` (actual Shell611–638): fresh topology/pure saved-Player prevalidation, actual Player -> level quiet commits, and the real saved Camera/canonical temporary outer-pixel HUD current optical gate. The new recipient remains nonplayable. `_floor_positive` at 541 requires exact saved Player and all nine local roots/Actor19/Scheduler/fields/consumers, public snapshot/context prevalidation and real current candidate optics. The older `_direct_native_candidate` is unused by this branch because it hardcodes beat1 and six activated recipients.

The recipient's actual FungalArt, overlay node, PlaneMesh and material must differ from the donor's handles. The immutable `SilverFloor` preload is legitimately shared by Godot's resource cache: both worlds must retain the actual known texture handle/path/64×64 dimensions, rather than requiring a false per-world texture distinction. Actual art `binding_error` and full-parent resource/world/callback guards remain authority. A candidate's public live writer always refuses even when valid, so that refusal is asserted as its nonplayable control, never counted as a floor-negative result.

The quiet listeners are deliberately attached AFTER `_prepare_snapshot`. They observe zero gameplay/native callback events during subsequent pure negative/recovery queries only; they do not retroactively establish silence during its prior canonical construction/quiet commit. No additional private direct-construction recipe is copied. Normal `_dispose` is used afterward, and donor native/effects/UI/disk/current snapshot identities are checked again. Candidate disposal notifications are not called quiet query events.

## Eleven independent faults, twice

`_floor_cases` at 557 applies exactly one fault to each actual world in turn: alpha-scissor threshold; AA mode; AA edge; blend mode; depth draw mode; hide; translate; detach; equivalent plane; equivalent material; equivalent texture pixels. Five settings test the newly extended material inventory independently. Mode choices use published named BaseMaterial3D constants: `ALPHA_ANTIALIASING_ALPHA_TO_COVERAGE`, `BLEND_MODE_ADD`, `DEPTH_DRAW_DISABLED`; thresholds/edge use the actual retained value plus .125. The current/off enums and defaults are checked through native readback. See [official BaseMaterial3D enums](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_basematerial3d.html). Renderer support of AA is not inferred from a resource property's readback.

Equivalent resources preserve existing plane size, the actual material's texture, and exact source image data/size. They are new in-memory test Resource handles only: no image file is edited, cropped, imported or produced. No physical CollisionShape is detached. Art leaf removal/readdition restores the same node at its original child index to preserve the exact retained composition; no native shape-owner registration is repaired. Each fault is restored synchronously before assertions/early return, with no yield while malformed. Only that fault's original value/reference/transform/parent index is restored; retained inventories are never re-pinned.

Each of 11 faults in donor and recipient records three meaningful assertions (66 loop checks plus unchanged setup/positive controls):

1. Actual changed readback; art/full runtime guard rejection; public `camera_framing_points` refusal PLUS nonempty diagnostic; empty actual local capture; public normal/context preflight rejection; `restore_state` false before commit; candidate current optical rejection as applicable. Installed authoritative Shell capture must be empty. Candidate uses the actual local producer/prevalidation/canonical restored optics, because its live writer is already forbidden at baseline.
2. Exact before/after native Player, all19 pure source states, Scheduler, fields/consumers, stable actual identities and lease/clock state, donor input/UI/attempts/all fixture disk, actual effect/public policy/audio node state, Camera transform and gameplay/native event counts.
3. After restoring originals, same leaf readback, actual native guards/current view, exact pristine Player/local writer and whole installed Shell snapshot recover, with no native/callback changes.

Public CinderLevel framing filters raw INF to `[]` and sets `last_camera_framing_error` (level59–68); `[]` alone is not accepted as a denial. No future-fit query substitutes for current containment, no point is removed, and no plane corner is newly declared a threat/collision authority.

## Purity boundaries and limits

`_floor_donor_observation` at 639 reads all files in the unique fixture user directory as raw `PackedByteArray`, including settings/preferences, campaign primary/backup and any extant temporary file. It also reads Attempts, actual World/Hero/Scheduler/actor/body/art/cue/field/consumer identities, native exact snapshots, current canonical menu/HUD/camera/input values, original action/checkpoint/completion/contact observers and AudioServer bus configuration. It does not call the authoritative full capture while malformed, since that separately tested refusal legitimately sets Shell/Level diagnostics. Expected error strings are retained, never erased or reset; they are excluded from simulation/UI/disk purity claims.

`_floor_effects_observation` at 624 uses public `policy_snapshot` plus actual effect-tree node identities/parenting/transforms/visibility/process mode and AudioStreamPlayer state/stream identity/bus/pitch/volume. It deliberately avoids the three active-count getters in effects344–357, which prune private registries. This is honest observable FX purity, not a fabricated private FX/RNG/clock snapshot. No new effect/action is requested. Candidate canonical optical checks may prepare that candidate Camera and ephemeral HUD exactly as the shared routine defines; their returned pose is required unchanged, and donor aliases/presentation are never supplied as its world authority.

Final report/summary explicitly labels pristine floor-resource guards: no active Warning/lease, ordinary defeat, full route, Title Continue, Retry, profile/kit, floor pixel/art fidelity, human fairness or FPS acceptance. The floor's y.002 depth/contact-shadow/contrast risks still need affected actual portrait review. The new guard checks do not finish the floor art or claim campaign acceptance.

